    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e86de41b-dde6-3a81-85b9-8ca61b90eeb9",
                "word": "eonism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df66273a-84fe-3d45-96ae-fc4078bdfc90",
                        "entry_id": "e86de41b-dde6-3a81-85b9-8ca61b90eeb9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The pretence of being the opposite sex, especially that by a man of being a woman; transvestism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad6b10e5-c0c7-4ffc-953d-db3314967b45",
                                "sense_id": "df66273a-84fe-3d45-96ae-fc4078bdfc90",
                                "text": "The chief of these intermediate sexual anomalies are: (1) physical hermaphroditism in its various stages; (2) gynandromorphism, or eunuchoidism, in which men possess characters resembling those of males who have been early castrated and women possess similarly masculine characters; (3) sexo-esthetic inversion, or Eonism (Hirschfeld's transvestism or cross-dressing), in which, outside the specifically sexual emotions, men possess the tastes of women and women those of men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78323b3a-10f3-4847-aed0-b107a8d969b6",
                                "sense_id": "df66273a-84fe-3d45-96ae-fc4078bdfc90",
                                "text": "Ellis seems, however, to regard this 'less common but more complete' type as embodying the essence of eonism, and he objected to the term transvestism because it focused attention solely on the element of cross-dressing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7f335a9-ec00-4457-98c5-ffbed38468bc",
                                "sense_id": "df66273a-84fe-3d45-96ae-fc4078bdfc90",
                                "text": "2013, C. N. Armstrong, 12: Transvestism, D. Robertson Smith, William M. Davidson (editors), Symposium on Nuclear Sex, Elsevier (Butterworth-Heinemann), page 88,\nHomosexuals do not as a rule want to change their sex and identity. This is the fundamental anomaly in eonism."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "638d4129-116b-40a4-84f6-446613f70cf9",
                        "source_entry_id": "e86de41b-dde6-3a81-85b9-8ca61b90eeb9",
                        "source_sense_id": "df66273a-84fe-3d45-96ae-fc4078bdfc90",
                        "source_sense_description": "pretence of being the opposite sex — see also transvestism",
                        "target_lang_word": "éonisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "éonisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "201b5087-a108-33e3-a839-676eec449ec8",
                                        "entry_id": "d31a512a-223d-308e-989f-e615fd4b0453",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte d’hérésie chrétienne du XIIᵉ siècle en Bretagne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f0db339-3e3e-40e2-a13a-f9523277183d",
                                                "sense_id": "201b5087-a108-33e3-a839-676eec449ec8",
                                                "text": "[…] on a cherché à étouffer l’éonisme en en faisant un incident de parcours au milieu des diverses hérésies de l’époque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a68cd168-0c7e-4bfe-b98f-feea0e0ef228",
                                                "sense_id": "201b5087-a108-33e3-a839-676eec449ec8",
                                                "text": "Certains d’entre eux subissent la torture et le bûcher plutôt que de renier l’Éonisme. Quand Éon et ses disciples se réfugiaient dans la forêt de Brocéliande après leurs expéditions punitives, ils se comportaient comme leurs ancêtres britons."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e073a08a-3b48-3af1-b479-99c650503cac",
                                        "entry_id": "d31a512a-223d-308e-989f-e615fd4b0453",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Travestisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08f7374b-d624-4144-bb15-81ad6d3e2ad3",
                                                "sense_id": "e073a08a-3b48-3af1-b479-99c650503cac",
                                                "text": "Enfin Harry Benjamin donne au mot la forme de transsexualism ^([sic]) qui va s’imposer en une dizaine d’années pour décrire une condition bien particulière, différente du transvestisme ou éonisme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4077a813-099d-4223-8074-c4e4dc430b1e",
                                                "sense_id": "e073a08a-3b48-3af1-b479-99c650503cac",
                                                "text": "Ce jeune homme était donc la mère de cette fille guère plus jeune et l’épouse de l’homme qui lui avait confessé un éonisme chronique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf7d1f27-da96-4bd4-abe8-946705684787",
                                                "sense_id": "e073a08a-3b48-3af1-b479-99c650503cac",
                                                "text": "Au qualificatif un peu cru de « trav », ils cherchent à substituer un euphémisme qui leur paraisse plus aimable et parlent d’éonisme. À cause du chevalier d’Éon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
